class.description:
A [TextureAtlas] references exactly one [Texture2D] (the sprite sheet, see [member texture]) and maps sprite names to rectangles in pixels of that texture (see [member regions]). The regions may have any size. Each region is available by name as an [AtlasTexture] through [method get_texture]; these textures always reference the atlas texture and are updated when the atlas changes.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var atlas: TextureAtlas = load("res://ui/icons.atlas.tres")
$Icon.texture = atlas.get_texture("coin")
$Player.sprite_frames = atlas.create_sprite_frames("walk_")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var atlas = GD.Load<TextureAtlas>("res://ui/icons.atlas.tres");
GetNode<Sprite2D>("Icon").Texture = atlas.GetTexture("coin");
GetNode<AnimatedSprite2D>("Player").SpriteFrames = atlas.CreateSpriteFrames("walk_");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
Besides [code].tres[/code], an atlas is read from and written to three fixed text layouts and can import TexturePacker JSON files (Hash and Array), the sprite sheet format used by Phaser and PixiJS:
[b]JSON[/b] ([method save_as_json], [method load_from_json]): an object with the keys [code]TexturePath[/code] and [code]AtlasImages[/code]; [code]AtlasImages[/code] maps each sprite name to an object with [code]X[/code], [code]Y[/code], [code]Width[/code] and [code]Height[/code], in region order. Unknown keys are ignored.
[codeblock lang=text]
{
	"TexturePath": "res://ui/icons.png",
	"AtlasImages": {
		"My_Sprite": { "X": 0, "Y": 0, "Width": 100, "Height": 100 },
		"Coin": { "X": 100, "Y": 0, "Width": 32, "Height": 32 }
	}
}
[/codeblock]
[b]CSV[/b] ([method save_as_csv], [method load_from_csv]): the first row is [code]TexturePath,<path>[/code], the second row the column names [code]Name,X,Y,Width,Height[/code], then one row per sprite.
[b]INI[/b] ([method save_as_ini], [method load_from_ini]): a section [code][Atlas][/code] with the key [code]TexturePath[/code], then one section per sprite with the keys [code]X[/code], [code]Y[/code], [code]Width[/code] and [code]Height[/code].
All three layouts have the optional keys (or columns) [code]MarginX[/code], [code]MarginY[/code], [code]SourceWidth[/code] and [code]SourceHeight[/code] for regions with a margin (see [method set_region_margin]); they are written only for regions that have one. CSV rows and INI sections are read and written with the same rules as the text formats of [ResourceTextSerializer] (quoting, comments, byte order mark).
Loading is all-or-nothing: the text is parsed and every region is validated first. On an error, the atlas is not changed and the error message names the sprite.
[b]Note:[/b] Like other resources, a [TextureAtlas] is not thread-safe. Use it from one thread at a time.

method.description:
Adds the region [param name] or changes its rectangle. A new region is appended to the order. The width and height must be greater than [code]0[/code], and if [member texture] is set, the rectangle must lie completely inside it (the size is taken from [method Texture2D.get_size], no pixels are read). Otherwise an error is printed, [constant ERR_INVALID_PARAMETER] is returned and nothing changes. See [method is_valid_region_name] for valid names.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var atlas = TextureAtlas.new()
atlas.texture = load("res://ui/icons.png")
atlas.set_region("coin", Rect2i(0, 0, 16, 16))
atlas.set_region("sword", Rect2i(16, 0, 24, 48))
$Coin.texture = atlas.get_texture("coin")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var atlas = new TextureAtlas();
atlas.Texture = GD.Load<Texture2D>("res://ui/icons.png");
atlas.SetRegion("coin", new Rect2I(0, 0, 16, 16));
atlas.SetRegion("sword", new Rect2I(16, 0, 24, 48));
GetNode<Sprite2D>("Coin").Texture = atlas.GetTexture("coin");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
